WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.370
-Facebook has had
an absolutely disastrous week,

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:06.806
with a damning whistleblower
interview on Sunday,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:09.008
an unprecedented outage
on Monday,

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.609
and then a Senate hearing
yesterday

00:00:10.609 --> 00:00:12.879
on how the company
dismantled safeguards

00:00:12.879 --> 00:00:14.614
and fostered a business model

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.949
where dangerous misinformation
can spread.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.319
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.990
Things have not been going great

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.660
for the world's most powerful
social-media platform.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.095
On Sunday a whistleblower

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.830
who filed complaints
against the company

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.100
with federal law enforcement
revealed herself on "60 Minutes"

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:36.336
and said the company
is aware of the harm it causes

00:00:36.336 --> 00:00:38.337
and prioritizes profits
over safety.

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:41.040
On Monday, Facebook
and its family of apps,

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:42.508
including WhatsApp
and Instagram,

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.410
suffered unprecedented outages.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.278
And on Tuesday,
the same whistleblower

00:00:46.278 --> 00:00:47.713
testified before Congress

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:50.283 line:0%
and said the company's products
harm children

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.184 line:0%
and hides what it knows
from the public.

00:00:52.184 --> 00:00:54.120 line:0%
Suffice it to say, Facebook
has had a [bleep] week.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:58.391
It's the kind of week you'd
normally post about on Facebook.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.326
Facebook had a worse week
than the Yankees

00:01:00.326 --> 00:01:04.063
or, worse yet, Yankees
radio announcer John Sterling.

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.631
-The pitch to Stanton.

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:07.332
There it goes.
Deep left.

00:01:07.332 --> 00:01:09.401
It is high, it is far.

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:12.538
It is gone out of the ballpark.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:15.809
A Stantonian home run.

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.945
Now, what did I do wrong?

00:01:19.945 --> 00:01:22.281
What did I see wrong?

00:01:22.281 --> 00:01:23.716
He's at first base.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:26.953
-Look, sports broadcasting
is hard,

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.288
and I also thought
it was gone off the bat,

00:01:29.288 --> 00:01:33.126
but why did he keep going after
the ball bounced off the wall?

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:36.795
"It is high, it is far,
it is gone.

00:01:36.795 --> 00:01:39.299
Stanton hit it so hard,
he stopped at first base,

00:01:39.299 --> 00:01:41.334
taunting the Red Sox,
as if to say,

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:45.371
'I will finish my home run trot
when I am good and ready.'

00:01:45.371 --> 00:01:47.974
What did I do?

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:49.909
What did I see?"

00:01:52.111 --> 00:01:55.148
I'm sorry, but I just had to
make some time tonight

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:57.550
to indulge some
Yankee schadenfreude.

00:01:57.550 --> 00:02:00.219
Plus, someone needs to
take Wally down a peg.

00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:03.822
He's such a big Yankees fan,
he wears 27 World Series rings.

00:02:03.822 --> 00:02:06.492
-That's right --
10 on my fingers, 10 on my toes,

00:02:06.492 --> 00:02:09.828
and seven on my --
-No!

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:12.064
No, I do feel a little bad
making fun of Wally

00:02:12.064 --> 00:02:15.368
on a day like today, until
I remember he is a Yankees fan

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:19.372
and a Patriots fan,
i.e., pure evil.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.573
You know what his
least favorite team is?

00:02:21.573 --> 00:02:25.145
The run that has to win
to save the orphanage.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:30.783
So just be happy that the only
Wally smiling last night

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.685
was this guy.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.221
Anyway, the massive
Facebook outage on Monday

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.223
was the company's worst
since 2008,

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:40.526
leaving its 3 billion-plus users
across the world in the dark

00:02:40.526 --> 00:02:42.862
while it tried to figure out
what the hell was going on.

00:02:42.862 --> 00:02:44.964
-Six hours later,
Facebook and Instagram

00:02:44.964 --> 00:02:46.865
finally back online tonight,

00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:50.203
the longest worldwide outage
ever to hit the company

00:02:50.203 --> 00:02:52.271
and its more than
3 billion users.

00:02:52.271 --> 00:02:54.373
The crash impacting businesses

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:56.943
who depend on the apps
to reach its customers.

00:02:56.943 --> 00:02:58.844
-Now, for many small businesses,

00:02:58.844 --> 00:03:00.513
Facebook serves
as their website,

00:03:00.513 --> 00:03:02.147
their way to share their hours

00:03:02.147 --> 00:03:04.116
and any updates
about their businesses.

00:03:04.116 --> 00:03:07.520
Especially in India,
Latin America, and in Africa,

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:08.854
Facebook, in a lot of ways,

00:03:08.854 --> 00:03:11.757
effectively functions
like the mobile Internet.

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:15.661
-Look, in certain countries,
Facebook is almost a utility

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:18.163
and it does provide
essential services,

00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:20.633
linkages around the world.

00:03:20.633 --> 00:03:22.668
-And it is, to say the least,
not good

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:24.670
that what amounts to
a global public utility

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.105
is controlled by one massive,

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:27.906
secretive international
conglomerate.

00:03:27.906 --> 00:03:30.743
It's like finding out that all
the drinking water in the world

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:33.679
is controlled by some company
called AquaBuds

00:03:33.679 --> 00:03:35.514
and it's run by
one weird little dude

00:03:35.514 --> 00:03:37.116
who created the company
out of revenge

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.885
because none of the cute girls
at his college

00:03:38.885 --> 00:03:40.152
would give him a glass of water.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.188
"Oh, I'll show them.
I'll show them all.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:44.657
Who's thirsty now, Courtney?"

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:47.293
Facebook has since explained
the outage, sort of.

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:49.161
They did so in
the vaguest way possible.

00:03:49.161 --> 00:03:51.797
Using as much tech gobbledygook
as they could,

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:54.767
a Facebook executive said
the outage was caused by...

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:04.610
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:07.346
Explain it to me
like I'm a Facebook user.

00:04:07.346 --> 00:04:08.848
Okay, I get it now.

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:12.017
Look, phrasing like "backbone
routers" and "data centers"

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:13.719
lead me to believe that
even when a company

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:15.120
as big as Facebook goes down,

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:18.758
they still have to deal with
Time Warner for some reason.

00:04:18.758 --> 00:04:20.626
"Yeah, so leave it unplugged
for 20 seconds

00:04:20.626 --> 00:04:21.627
before plugging it back in.

00:04:21.627 --> 00:04:22.828
All right, I'll try it."

00:04:22.828 --> 00:04:24.129
Anyway, the point is

00:04:24.129 --> 00:04:25.864
that no one company
should have this much power --

00:04:25.864 --> 00:04:27.566
not just one company,
one person,

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.135
because as whistleblower
Frances Haugen

00:04:30.135 --> 00:04:31.570
explained
at yesterday's hearing,

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:32.739
there is one person

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.707
who very much calls the shots
at Facebook.

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:38.477
-Mark holds a very unique role
in the tech industry

00:04:38.477 --> 00:04:44.183
in that he holds over 55% of all
the voting shares for Facebook.

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.185
There are no similarly
powerful companies

00:04:46.185 --> 00:04:49.755
that are as
unilaterally controlled,

00:04:49.755 --> 00:04:51.824
and in the end,
the buck stops with Mark.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:55.094
There's no one currently holding
Mark accountable but himself.

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:58.597
Mark has built an organization
that is very metrics-driven.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:05:00.633
It is intended to be flat.

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:03.169
There is no
unilateral responsibility.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.003
The metrics make the decision.

00:05:05.003 --> 00:05:08.007
Unfortunately,
that itself is a decision.

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:11.844
And in the end, if he is the CEO
and the chairman of Facebook,

00:05:11.844 --> 00:05:14.246
he is responsible
for those decisions.

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:15.681
-The buck stops with him.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:16.916
-The buck stops with him.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.517
-That's right --
The buck stops with him,

00:05:18.517 --> 00:05:22.521
which is, I guess, why, when he
goes out, he wears a disguise.

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:24.923
Either he's wearing
too much sunscreen

00:05:24.923 --> 00:05:27.025
or his face is at home
recharging.

00:05:27.025 --> 00:05:29.995
I knew there were funny clowns
and sad clowns,

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:32.665
but I didn't know
there were neutral clowns.

00:05:32.665 --> 00:05:34.333
"I made you a balloon animal."

00:05:34.333 --> 00:05:36.702
"Oh, what kind of animal
is this?"

00:05:36.702 --> 00:05:39.472
"It is the double helix,
representing a DNA molecule,

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.607
so really it could be
any animal on Earth.

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:43.642
Happy birth anniversary day."

00:05:43.642 --> 00:05:45.845
Haugen claims that Zuckerberg
made the choice

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:47.980
to run the site
based on the metrics alone,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:50.449
which, if true,
is itself a massive choice.

00:05:50.449 --> 00:05:52.552
You don't get to dodge
responsibility by saying,

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:55.354
"It's not me promoting
anti-vax misinformation.

00:05:55.354 --> 00:05:56.755
It's a math equation."

00:05:56.755 --> 00:05:58.958
The rest of us don't get to
show up to work three hours late

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.860
and say, "It's not my fault
Waze told me the fastest route

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.429
was kayaking up the East River.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.297
I ran aground on a dead mobster.

00:06:05.297 --> 00:06:09.168
Oh, Jimmy, why'd you have to
talk to the cops?"

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:11.270
So if the buck stops
with Zuckerberg,

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.673
what was he doing as
a whistleblower came forward

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:15.474
with damning allegations
that his company

00:06:15.474 --> 00:06:17.576
was knowingly harming people
for profit?

00:06:17.576 --> 00:06:19.512
-As this whistleblower
came forward this week,

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:21.313
Facebook CEO Mark Zuckerberg

00:06:21.313 --> 00:06:23.983
was posting video
of his sailing trip

00:06:23.983 --> 00:06:26.652
as his company
faced a firestorm.

00:06:26.652 --> 00:06:29.822
-The hearing also took stark aim
at Facebook's CEO,

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:33.926
Mark Zuckerberg, who posted
a video sailing with his family

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:36.796
on Sunday
just before Haugen exposed

00:06:36.796 --> 00:06:39.164
some of the company's research
on children

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:42.167
in an explosive
"60 Minutes" interview.

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.703
-Side note -- I don't know
how this guy's always outdoors

00:06:44.703 --> 00:06:45.805
with his complexion.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:47.506
If I spend five minutes
on the beach,

00:06:47.506 --> 00:06:49.975
I end up with sand in
every orifice for three days

00:06:49.975 --> 00:06:51.644
and a sunburn on my taint.

00:06:51.644 --> 00:06:53.613
I don't know how.

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:55.815
I do know if you go to Walgreens

00:06:55.815 --> 00:06:57.983
and ask the pharmacist for help
with a sunburnt taint,

00:06:57.983 --> 00:06:59.084
they kick you out of the store,

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:02.622
which, if you ask me,
"taint" polite.

00:07:02.622 --> 00:07:04.757
But that's definitely
where you want to be

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.125
when a whistleblower accuses you

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:08.194
of manipulating people
for profit -- sailing.

00:07:08.194 --> 00:07:11.997
What's the matter, you couldn't
find a dressage horse?

00:07:11.997 --> 00:07:16.201
"I take issue with the fact that
you're criticizing our company."

00:07:16.201 --> 00:07:18.337
Then on Tuesday,
Zuckerberg emerged

00:07:18.337 --> 00:07:20.039
to respond to the claims
from Haugen.

00:07:20.039 --> 00:07:22.407
And suffice it to say
his rebuttal was not that great.

00:07:22.407 --> 00:07:23.910
-Zuckerberg writes...

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:43.462
-You don't know a tech company
that sets out to build a product

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:44.997
that makes people angry
or depressed?

00:07:44.997 --> 00:07:47.199
What about Adobe Flash Player?

00:07:47.199 --> 00:07:49.034
Gen-Zers won't know
what I'm talking about,

00:07:49.034 --> 00:07:50.502
but it used to be
anytime you wanted

00:07:50.502 --> 00:07:51.737
to watch something
on the Internet,

00:07:51.737 --> 00:07:53.872
like a dancing baby
or a funny chipmunk,

00:07:53.872 --> 00:07:56.775
you had to update something
called Adobe Flash Player

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:59.211
that you didn't
even know you had.

00:07:59.211 --> 00:08:00.880
And it sucked
because it took forever

00:08:00.880 --> 00:08:02.048
and you had to do it every time.

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:03.816
And even
the error message said...

00:08:06.485 --> 00:08:07.786
Or how about Twitter?

00:08:07.786 --> 00:08:09.455
Angry and depressed
is their whole business model.

00:08:09.455 --> 00:08:11.056
I have a Klonopin
set aside every night

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:12.491
for my pre-bed doom scrolling.

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:14.360
I have specific accounts
I check every day

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:15.761
just to get pissed off.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:17.963
When you used to log on
to Twitter, the bird whistled,

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:19.498
and now it just curses at you.

00:08:19.498 --> 00:08:21.166
-[Bleep] you.
[ Tweets ]

00:08:21.166 --> 00:08:24.637
-Also, you think
advertisers care

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:27.005
if the content people
engage with the most

00:08:27.005 --> 00:08:28.340
is angry and depressing?

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:30.209
Advertisers just want eyeballs.

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:32.345
If they only wanted happy people
to see their ads,

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:35.314
they sure as hell wouldn't
put billboards in Times Square.

00:08:35.314 --> 00:08:36.982
Times Square's
the only place on Earth

00:08:36.982 --> 00:08:41.053
you can hear Elmo call a kid a
dip[bleep] in a Russian accent.

00:08:41.053 --> 00:08:43.723
[ Russian accent ] No tickle me.
I tickle you.

00:08:43.723 --> 00:08:46.191
Elmo tickle you.

00:08:46.191 --> 00:08:48.027
[ Normal voice ] There's nothing
advertisers love more

00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:49.595
than commercials
during sports games.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:52.364
Those make people more angry
and depressed than anything.

00:08:52.364 --> 00:08:55.400
Is Budweiser worried Wally's
never gonna drink it again

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.835
just because one of their
commercials played

00:08:56.835 --> 00:08:58.437
after Aaron Judge
was thrown out at home?

00:08:58.437 --> 00:08:59.505
I'm sorry, Wally.

00:08:59.505 --> 00:09:01.139
-Actually, Seth,
I don't drink Budweiser.

00:09:01.139 --> 00:09:02.308
-Oh, because of the commercial?

00:09:02.308 --> 00:09:04.310
-No, because I get paid per line
on this show.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.011
I only drink champagne.

00:09:06.011 --> 00:09:09.715
-[ Laughs ] Oh!

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:13.386
Audiences are coming back,
Wally, and the party's over.

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:17.256
[ Laughs ]

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:22.261
So Zuckerberg likes to present
a glowing portrait

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:23.562
of what his platform does,

00:09:23.562 --> 00:09:25.897
but in reality what Facebook
hides from the public

00:09:25.897 --> 00:09:29.035
it's much more revealing,
as CNN explained this morning.

00:09:29.035 --> 00:09:33.972
-Facebook released these numbers
for the second quarter of 2021

00:09:33.972 --> 00:09:36.042
sort of painting a rosy picture

00:09:36.042 --> 00:09:39.979
that showed the best-performing
links and posts on the platform

00:09:39.979 --> 00:09:43.281
were about nice things
like your pets and cooking

00:09:43.281 --> 00:09:46.118
and family outings
and things like that.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:47.386
But some people started to ask,

00:09:47.386 --> 00:09:49.321
"Well, what did quarter one
look like?

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:50.489
What did the first quarter --

00:09:50.489 --> 00:09:52.124
the first three months
of this year look like?"

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:54.193
And it eventually --
That report,

00:09:54.193 --> 00:09:56.529
which Facebook
chose not to release,

00:09:56.529 --> 00:09:58.164
was leaked to
"The New York Times,"

00:09:58.164 --> 00:10:01.467
and it showed one
of the top-performing links

00:10:01.467 --> 00:10:04.070
on the platform in
the first quarter of this year

00:10:04.070 --> 00:10:06.905
was a piece undermining
the vaccine.

00:10:06.905 --> 00:10:08.374
-They hid that report
from the public,

00:10:08.374 --> 00:10:10.042
but even if
it didn't eventually leak,

00:10:10.042 --> 00:10:12.444
you don't need to be a data
analyst to know that Facebook

00:10:12.444 --> 00:10:15.180
can be a toxic stew
of conspiracy nonsense,

00:10:15.180 --> 00:10:17.282
and that's part
of the business model.

00:10:17.282 --> 00:10:19.151
Just talk to your weird uncle
about the news.

00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:20.852
"Are you getting the vaccine,
Uncle Ron?"

00:10:20.852 --> 00:10:23.756
"Well, I read on Facebook
that it has a microchip in it

00:10:23.756 --> 00:10:25.958
that turns your penis
into a Wi-Fi hotspot,

00:10:25.958 --> 00:10:27.192
so I'm 50/50."

00:10:27.192 --> 00:10:29.495
No corporation,
let alone a single individual,

00:10:29.495 --> 00:10:31.564
should have this much power
over how we communicate,

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:33.265
which is why progressives
like Bernie Sanders,

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:35.567
Elizabeth Warren,
and Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez

00:10:35.567 --> 00:10:37.503
have been calling
for a while now

00:10:37.503 --> 00:10:39.738
to break up these giant
tech monopolies.

00:10:39.738 --> 00:10:43.175
-I think we need vigorous
antitrust legislation

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.644
in this country,
because you are seeing --

00:10:45.644 --> 00:10:47.879
you name the area,
whether it's pharmaceuticals,

00:10:47.879 --> 00:10:51.116
whether it is Wall Street,
whether it is high tech,

00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:54.586
fewer and fewer
gigantic corporations

00:10:54.586 --> 00:10:55.921
owning those sectors.

00:10:55.921 --> 00:10:58.924
Facebook has un-- I mean,
we deal with it every day.

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:01.226
They determine who
we can communicate with.

00:11:01.226 --> 00:11:04.096
They have incredible power
over the economy,

00:11:04.096 --> 00:11:05.731
over the political life
of this country,

00:11:05.731 --> 00:11:07.332
in a very dangerous sense.

00:11:07.332 --> 00:11:09.201
-Anybody in here
a little worried

00:11:09.201 --> 00:11:11.170
about how Facebook
uses your data?

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.204
[ Crowd cheering ]

00:11:12.204 --> 00:11:14.439
Yeah, just a little bit worried.

00:11:14.439 --> 00:11:16.242
So some of you may know,

00:11:16.242 --> 00:11:20.279
there was another company
that came along, WhatsApp,

00:11:20.279 --> 00:11:21.947
and they said,
"We're going to offer you

00:11:21.947 --> 00:11:23.282
a lot more data privacy.

00:11:23.282 --> 00:11:27.886
That's going to be a part
of our sales pitch here,"

00:11:27.886 --> 00:11:31.156
and, boy, they started
getting customers.

00:11:31.156 --> 00:11:34.326
So Facebook had a choice.

00:11:34.326 --> 00:11:39.698
Facebook could, A,
get better on privacy

00:11:39.698 --> 00:11:42.600
or, B, they could just buy out
the competition.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.771
What did Facebook choose?
Just buy out the competition.

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:47.105
No.

00:11:47.105 --> 00:11:50.876
Giants are not allowed
to buy out the competition.

00:11:50.876 --> 00:11:54.646
The competition has to be given
a chance to thrive, grow,

00:11:54.646 --> 00:11:57.983
and either the giant gets better
or the giant dies.

00:11:57.983 --> 00:11:59.218
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:59.218 --> 00:12:01.086
-Whenever Warren
goes into teacher mode,

00:12:01.086 --> 00:12:03.255
it makes me wish she'd been
my driver's ed instructor.

00:12:03.255 --> 00:12:04.622
Then I'd know
how to parallel park.

00:12:04.622 --> 00:12:06.925
"Who here thinks you're
supposed to go in headfirst?

00:12:06.925 --> 00:12:08.060
Well, you're wrong.

00:12:08.060 --> 00:12:09.294
You want to pull in backwards

00:12:09.294 --> 00:12:11.229
at a 45-degree angle
toward the curb.

00:12:11.229 --> 00:12:12.797
And if you don't use
your turn signal,

00:12:12.797 --> 00:12:14.600
so help me God,
I will fail you."

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.201
No company should
have this much power,

00:12:16.201 --> 00:12:18.070
which is why progressives
have been calling for years

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.272
to break up Facebook
and other tech giants.

00:12:20.272 --> 00:12:22.441
If the testimony we've heard
this week is correct,

00:12:22.441 --> 00:12:24.176
Facebook knows what it's doing
is dangerous,

00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:26.177
no matter how much they play
innocent and say...

00:12:26.177 --> 00:12:27.947
-What did I do wrong?

00:12:27.947 --> 00:12:30.949
-[ Laughs ]

00:12:30.949 --> 00:12:33.452
"Is it my eyes?

00:12:33.452 --> 00:12:35.754
My ears?"

00:12:35.754 --> 00:12:37.423
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:12:41.259 --> 00:12:42.394
God's Love We Deliver

00:12:42.394 --> 00:12:44.296
cooks and brings
over 2 million meals a year

00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:46.799
to men, women, and children
living with HIV/AIDS, cancer,

00:12:46.799 --> 00:12:48.066
and other serious illnesses.

00:12:48.066 --> 00:12:49.968
They need your help
now more than ever.

00:12:49.968 --> 00:12:52.204
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the "donate" button.

00:12:52.204 --> 00:12:54.940
Stay safe, get vaccinated.
We love you.

